    {
      "id": 4,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Primary scalable candidate: replace dense companion-matrix powering with exact Kitamasa polynomial exponentiation. Compute x^(H-1) modulo the recurrence characteristic polynomial, then combine its coefficients with A1..AN in O(N^2 log H); use dynamic O(N) storage. Independently verify ordering/indexing on N=1, H=N+1, zeros, and values near the modulus.\",\"B\":\"Develop an independent generating-function/Bostan-Mori solution. Construct the correct numerator from the base terms and denominator 1-P1*x-...-PN*x^N, then use parity halving with exact modular polynomial products. Avoid approximate transforms; retain this candidate only if its complete-program cost beats the simpler recurrence method.\",\"C\":\"Own a low-latency hybrid candidate. Use a rolling direct recurrence when H-N is genuinely small and a cache-friendly quadratic exponentiation path otherwise, with dispatch based only on input dimensions/work estimates. Eliminate fixed dense matrices and the source's unnecessary dense final matrix product; investigate guarded, race-free four-core polynomial kernels only where their overhead is repaid.\",\"G\":\"Treat A, B, and C as competing complete programs, not automatically additive patches. Validate each and any merge against broad oracle-style cases, especially coefficient orientation, modulo arithmetic, N=1, and boundary exponents. Measure repeated end-to-end runs on the ARM64 target against the valid 0.020203 s baseline; select the fastest correct whole candidate (including baseline if necessary) and only retain integration changes with independent evidence.\",\"analysis\":\"The valid baseline is very short (mean 0.020203 s, four correctness cases), so startup and parallel overhead may dominate measured inputs. Its source nevertheless performs full dense n-by-n companion matrix products and squarings, O(N^3 log H), plus a dense matrix-by-vector-in-disguise final product; this becomes tens of billions of operations near N=1020. Exact linear-recurrence methods provide the main scalable opportunity, while C explores generic low-gap and systems-cost cases. All candidates must preserve the input/output semantics for every valid input and must not hard-code expected results.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"1fe13217caf0e05e3174e89bdcf9fadf39257245a1fef69bbdd7cec7bb72fc0e\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Primary scalable candidate: replace dense companion-matrix powering with exact Kitamasa polynomial exponentiation. Compute x^(H-1) modulo the recurrence characteristic polynomial, then combine its coefficients with A1..AN in O(N^2 log H); use dynamic O(N) storage. Independently verify ordering/indexing on N=1, H=N+1, zeros, and values near the modulus.\",\"B\":\"Develop an independent generating-function/Bostan-Mori solution. Construct the correct numerator from the base terms and denominator 1-P1*x-...-PN*x^N, then use parity halving with exact modular polynomial products. Avoid approximate transforms; retain this candidate only if its complete-program cost beats the simpler recurrence method.\",\"C\":\"Own a low-latency hybrid candidate. Use a rolling direct recurrence when H-N is genuinely small and a cache-friendly quadratic exponentiation path otherwise, with dispatch based only on input dimensions/work estimates. Eliminate fixed dense matrices and the source's unnecessary dense final matrix product; investigate guarded, race-free four-core polynomial kernels only where their overhead is repaid.\",\"G\":\"Treat A, B, and C as competing complete programs, not automatically additive patches. Validate each and any merge against broad oracle-style cases, especially coefficient orientation, modulo arithmetic, N=1, and boundary exponents. Measure repeated end-to-end runs on the ARM64 target against the valid 0.020203 s baseline; select the fastest correct whole candidate (including baseline if necessary) and only retain integration changes with independent evidence.\",\"analysis\":\"The valid baseline is very short (mean 0.020203 s, four correctness cases), so startup and parallel overhead may dominate measured inputs. Its source nevertheless performs full dense n-by-n companion matrix products and squarings, O(N^3 log H), plus a dense matrix-by-vector-in-disguise final product; this becomes tens of billions of operations near N=1020. Exact linear-recurrence methods provide the main scalable opportunity, while C explores generic low-gap and systems-cost cases. All candidates must preserve the input/output semantics for every valid input and must not hard-code expected results.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-5.6-terra\",\"nonce\":\"9f20c2efeec64827a8199534f5635a51\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"1fe13217caf0e05e3174e89bdcf9fadf39257245a1fef69bbdd7cec7bb72fc0e\",\"session_id\":\"15219a6fd62b4dcb91b395dcd4ae03d5\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"4eacb9889b29ce14780226b513d090abf4dcc7a87389ccdac9daeeff105d2a83\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":10751,\"output_tokens\":6663,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":6214}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-5.6-terra\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"max\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":17414,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
